= Mussolini Arrested!

Following the end of the latest elections, we have been informed that Benito Mussolini, head of the relatively unknown FdC and former member of the PSI, has been arrested in Milan by local police, under allegation of harbouring illegal weapons as well as operating a violent organisation.

Mussolini has had multiple runs in with the law since 1902, starting with accidents in <span style="color: #dddddd;">**Swit**</span><span style="color: #DA291C;">**zer**</span><span style="color: #dddddd;">**land**</span> over crimes of vagrancy, attempting to start a general strike,  falsifying documents, illegal public assemblies, among other crimes.

However, this hasnt come without protests either, as a delegation  made of Richard Luzzato and Camillo Candiani, both respected figures within <span style="color: #008C45;">**It**</span><span style="color: #E5E4E2;">**ali**</span><span style="color: #CD212A;">**an**</span> politics, supported by Luigi Albertini, senator and member of the LDR, have taken their complaints to the police chief of Milan, however we still have the power to decide what we will do.

What should we do?

- @mussolini_justice: Keep him locked up and begin preparing for his trial.
- @root: Release him; don't let him become a martyr.

@mussolini_justice
subtitle: We can only hold him for so long. 
on-arrival: mussolini_jailed = 1; fdc_militancy += 0.08; fdc_strength += 7; mussolini_trial_timer = 12; veterans_pnf -= 3; middle_class_pnf -= 7; rural_pnf -= 4;

We keep Mussolini in prison, awaiting trial. His trial is to be in [+ mussolini_trial_timer +] months, and we should gather enough evidence to convict him by then.

In his absence however, the Fasci grow more and more rowdy, terrorising the local populace and gaining a notorious reputation for themselves.

- @interior_investigations: Let's get to work then, shall we?

@interior_investigations
